ORCA-MI Research Licence
Version 1.1

Copyright (c) 2026 Yazdan Salimi (salimiyazdan@gmail.com). All rights reserved.

"ORCA-MI" (Open Radiology & Computational Analysis - Molecular Imaging) means the
programs distributed in this repository (ORCA-MI.exe, the ORCA-MI installer),
the accompanying files (orcami.py, examples) and the documentation.
The Python helper orcami.py and the example scripts have their own, more
open terms: see section 2a.

1. Permitted use
   You may download, install and use ORCA-MI free of charge for
   non-commercial research and education, including academic and
   hospital research.

1a. Personal licence and trial
   Full use of ORCA-MI requires a personal licence file issued by the
   author, free of charge for the use described in section 1. A licence
   file is issued to one named person, is personal and may not be
   shared, transferred or published. It may be issued for a limited time.
   Without a licence file, ORCA-MI runs as a 7-day trial on each computer,
   with part of its functions; after the trial it cannot be used until a
   licence file is loaded. The author may refuse or withdraw a licence,
   in particular when these terms are not respected.

2. Not permitted
   Without prior written permission of the author you may not:
   a. use ORCA-MI commercially, including for paid services or in, or for
      the development of, a commercial product;
   b. sell, rent, lease or sublicense ORCA-MI;
   c. distribute modified copies of ORCA-MI, or reverse engineer,
      decompile or disassemble it, except as far as applicable law
      expressly permits this despite this restriction;
   d. remove or change the copyright, licence or research-use notices.
   You may share unmodified copies of the installer or the portable zip as
   published by the author, together with this licence, free of charge;
   licence files are personal (section 1a) and may not be shared.

2a. Python helper and example scripts
   orcami.py and the example scripts (the examples folder of the ORCA-MI
   repository and the copies installed with ORCA-MI) may be used, copied,
   modified and shared, also inside your own projects and publications,
   under the MIT licence printed at the end of this file. Section 2 does not
   apply to them. They only control ORCA-MI; using ORCA-MI itself remains
   under this licence.

3. No clinical use
   ORCA-MI is a research tool. It is not a medical device: it has no CE
   marking and no FDA clearance. It must not be used for diagnosis,
   treatment, treatment planning or any other clinical decision about a
   patient. All measurements, segmentations, dose estimates and AI results
   must be checked by a qualified person.

4. Citation
   Work that uses ORCA-MI and leads to a publication, presentation or
   report must cite ORCA-MI as described in CITATION.cff in the ORCA-MI
   repository, and acknowledge its author, Yazdan Salimi.

5. Third-party components
   ORCA-MI contains open-source libraries that remain under their own
   licences; these are listed, with their licence texts, in
   docs/third_party_licenses.html and in the program (Help -> About ->
   Third-party licences). Optional components that ORCA-MI downloads or
   installs on request (for example Python, PyTorch, nnU-Net,
   nnInteractive, MONAI and AI model weights) are covered by their own
   licences. The nnInteractive model weights, and every model fine-tuned
   from them, are licensed under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 (non-commercial use only).

5a. Data and privacy
   ORCA-MI works on your computer. It never sends images, patient data,
   DICOM headers or file names.
   a. A licence request sends what you type in the form (name, institution,
      e-mail address, country, intended use, the name you give the
      computer), a code of the computer (derived from Windows, not from
      hardware serial numbers), the Windows version and the ORCA-MI
      version, so that the licence file can be issued for that computer.
   b. Everything else is optional and asked for first, and can be changed
      at any time in Help -> Privacy & usage statistics: anonymous usage
      statistics (how often the program and its features are opened), the
      country of the computer (from the Windows region setting), checks for
      new versions and AI models, and, for licensed users, usage statistics
      linked to the licence (they can be withdrawn, and are then deleted).
   c. Bug reports and feedback are only sent when you press Send, with the
      text you can read before sending.
   This information is used only to issue licences, to improve ORCA-MI and
   to inform users; it is not sold or given to others. To see, correct or
   delete what is kept about you, contact the author.

6. No warranty, no liability
   ORCA-MI is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or
   implied, including the warranties of merchantability, fitness for a
   particular purpose and non-infringement. To the maximum extent
   permitted by law, the author is not liable for any claim, damage or
   other liability, including loss of data, arising from the use of, or
   the inability to use, ORCA-MI.

7. Termination
   This licence ends automatically if you do not comply with it. You must
   then stop using ORCA-MI and delete your copies.

